          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:936d307533bbe6ca1222f3a75f397e4a602aca1cb641d7ab11bac9485a06047b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_73aee9a3e0b14acc972ef047983f0fa9",
      "statement": "ProviderResolverTests builds the resolver directly with Options.Create and never reaches the network: it asserts distinctive message fragments rather than full text for the empty-list, duplicate-name, and missing-provider constructor failures, and only asserts NotNull on the created client; the default endpoint constant, the invalid-endpoint message, case-insensitive selection, the model id actually passed to GetChatClient, and disposal propagation remain unpinned.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/Sebastian.Tests/Agent/ProviderResolverTests.cs#L9-L77",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5e9b6fe9751a2f4c5396d1d9488c72e1b26ba5029391b6793a46a14b9731712:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_465c3bea8fe84951b609638971146aa1",
      "statement": "ProviderResolver is the only file in the agent layer that suppresses OPENAI001 alongside MEAI001, marking the OpenAI client surface as experimental and keeping that dependency isolated from the harness files that instead suppress MAAI001/MEAI001 — relevant because the build uses TreatWarningsAsErrors with AnalysisLevel=latest-all.",
